0..77 Comment "// Allocation permutation (Sterling, Gratzer and Birkedal, _Towards univalent"
78..153 Comment "// reference types_, CSL 2024, doi:10.4230/LIPIcs.CSL.2024.19, Fig. 2): two"
154..232 Comment "// allocations commute. A structure whose parts name each other by ids into an"
233..310 Comment "// arena is built twice, its nodes allocated in two orders, so the ids of one"
311..387 Comment "// arena are a relabelling of the other\'s. The relabelling is a path between"
388..460 Comment "// the id types; the links and the labels carried along it are the other"
461..535 Comment "// arena\'s, so the two arenas are one, and a consumer that walks the links"
536..556 Comment "// reads both alike."
558..630 Comment "/// The relabelling between the two allocation orders: the first two ids"
631..657 Comment "/// swap, the third stays."
